# calls, entries and returns lowered to the pieces the calling convention
# places them in
#
# the target's convention classifies every call at its signature and the
# number of its named arguments, every function's entry and every return at
# the function's own signature, once, and the pass rewrites each into piece
# form. a call becomes `call.placed`, a return `ret.placed` and the entry's
# parameters become its pieces, the body recording where each arrives. every
# operand of piece form is a scalar of at most a register's width, its place,
# scale and fill held as immediates, so nothing after the pass classifies
# again and no later legalisation of types touches it.
#
# memory carries what is not a scalar. a by-value aggregate is read piece by
# piece from the memory it was loaded from, at the point it was loaded, or
# from a stack slot it is stored to before the call. one that lies whole in
# the argument area, every piece a stack place one after the other, travels as
# one block instead where the target's bulk copy is native: the caller copies
# it to the area once, at the address `arg.outgoing` gives, and the callee
# reads it where it lies, at the address `arg.incoming` gives, so it has no
# piece in the signature and no register carries its words. a value passed by
# reference is copied to a stack slot the caller owns, and the piece is its
# address. a result returned by reference lands in a slot whose address the
# caller passes, and the callee rebuilds an incoming aggregate in a slot of
# its own, or reads the caller's copy of one by reference, at each use, so a
# store of a parameter is a copy between memories. the copies move whole
# words up to the target's bound and are one bulk copy past it, and a piece
# whose size no integer has is read and written in the widest words that fit
# it. a float piece of a size no format has travels as the narrowest format
# that holds it, its bytes read and written as an integer's and reinterpreted,
# as are a float's of a format the build holds no unit for, which the half
# precision legalisation has already made its encoding everywhere else. a
# vector no unit holds travels as an aggregate does, so the run of the vector
# legalisation after this pass takes apart its loads and stores and no vector
# it cannot hold is left at a boundary. a bulk copy the target has no
# instruction for is a loop the bulk legalisation makes after the pass
# (mirl.legal.bulk), and a function that requires constant time copies in
# words at any size there (mirl.legal.moves).
#
# a result returned by reference is built in place where nothing can tell. in
# the callee, a stack slot every return hands back whole, read just before it,
# whose address goes nowhere but its own loads and stores, is the memory the
# carrier addresses, so no return copies it. in the caller, a result whose one
# use stores it whole is passed that store's destination as its address when
# the destination is a stack slot whose address goes nowhere but its own loads
# and stores, which the callee cannot reach. any other keeps its slot and the
# copy, since the callee may read the destination through an argument, a
# global or a pointer it holds while it writes the result.
#
# a copy by reference is made each time the call or return it serves runs,
# since a callee may write its copy and a return's path may pass the copy
# another return makes to the result's slot: an aggregate is copied from the memory it was loaded from,
# at the load, when the load is in the call's or return's block and so runs
# once for each time that does, and any other value is stored whole just
# ahead of the call or return. every piece is made where it dominates the
# instruction it travels at.
#
# the pass reads no value to decide anything: every load, store and copy it
# makes follows from types and the convention alone, so it keeps constant
# time. every piece of a secret value is marked secret, and every address the
# pass forms, a slot, a pointer a value travels by reference through and an
# offset past either, is as secret as its base alone, so a secret value moved
# through memory forms no address from a secret.
#
# a rebuilt value stands at every point the value it replaces did, so the
# records that read the old one read it. an aggregate load the pass leaves
# unused goes, and each variable bound to it is bound to the storage it read,
# on the instruction that addresses that storage.
#
# a variadic call under a row whose unnamed arguments are x64's words, as
# arm64ec's, hands its callee the bytes of its stack words as one more piece,
# in the row's size register. the address of the first word is no value of
# the ir, so the call keeps its named count for the selection to set it.
#
# what it refuses: a piece extended by a signedness the ir does not state, a
# scalar split across pieces, and a piece in a register no piece type is made
# for, each naming its value.

